Rust Day 4: Variables & mutability. Why Rust won't let you change x, and how mut fixes it.

📌 In this short:
✅ Variables are immutable by default: let x = 5;
✅ Changing it gives error E0384: cannot assign twice to immutable variable
✅ let mut x = 5; makes it changeable, and tells readers it will change

💻 Code from the video:
fn main() {
    let mut x = 5;
    println!("{x}");
    x = 6;
    println!("{x}");
}

📖 Learn more: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch03-01-variables-and-mutability.html
